{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["וַתֵּלַהְ — like: וְתַכֵּה מִכַּעַס עֵינִי. The heh is the root letter; therefore it has a mapik heh. And likewise: נָגָהּ אוֹר." "אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם וְאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן — but the lands more distant than the land of Canaan did not come to the land of Egypt, because they were too far away — or perhaps there was not so great a famine there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "Rashbam cites ותכה מכעס עיני (Lamentations 2:11) as a parallel for the weak/extra heh form. 'מפיק ה״א' means the heh has a mappiq, indicating it is a consonantal root letter rather than a mater lectionis."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:28.998480309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}